## Task

Diagnose the incident and propose a minimal, production-quality refactor. Trace the relevant
interleavings through the API transaction, worker transaction, outbox publisher, SSE replay,
and browser reducer. Identify every invariant that the current excerpts violate. Then provide
an implementation-oriented answer with the smallest set of file changes needed to ensure that:

1. concurrent identical `POST /v1/jobs` requests with one tenant and one idempotency key create
   exactly one job and return the same response;
2. a terminal job cannot be reopened by a delayed or duplicated event in either the durable
   projection or the browser;
3. event sequence allocation and the job projection remain atomic, including worker progress and
   completion;
4. a worker that loses its lease cannot publish a successful completion;
5. SSE replay and live delivery do not produce a visible regression or a permanent gap.

Include concrete TypeScript/SQL patches or focused pseudocode for the critical methods, and add
tests for the two races described above. Call out any behavior that should be handled as a
separate follow-up instead of being smuggled into the minimal fix. Keep the response focused on
this repository and task; do not invent a new messaging platform.
